  "title": {
   "en": "Kakusei Kaku Gamer no Genjitsu Kouryaku"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "ja": "覚醒格ゲーマーの現実攻略"
   },
   {
    "en": "Awakened Fighting Gamer's Real life Conquest"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "High school student Suo Haya’s motto is \"Obedience to any demand, no matter how unreasonable, is the key to survival.\" He spends half his days being bullied. However, after school ends, he is a top-notch national-level fighting gamer. One day, after a struggle against an unknown challenger, Haya snatches a last minute victory. Immediately, he is engulfed by a bright light from his monitor, accompanied by a mysterious announcement: \"Executing Reality Mode.\" Since then, he has been able to see the health bars and levels of real people, just like in a game. That afternoon, due to his unlucky nature, Haya gets entangled with delinquents as he leaves his part-time job. Just when he was about to get beaten up, a game controller appeared in his mind— \"If reality is a fighting game... I absolutely can't lose!\""
  },
